# Platform Admin and Application registry (ticket 07).
# Create a Platform Admin first (after npm run build):
#   npm run platform-admin:create -- --email ops@example.com --first-name Ops --last-name Admin
# then log in as them with http/auth.http. Platform Admins have no Tenant, so no switch is needed.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:9800
@accessToken = paste-platform-admin-access-token
@applicationId = paste-application-id
@resourceTypeId = paste-resource-type-id
@actionId = paste-action-id

### Register an Application. The response holds clientSecret: shown this once, stored only as a hash.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Billing", "allowedOrigins": ["https://billing.example.com", "http://localhost:5173"] }

### Applications, newest first (paginated: limit, cursor)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### One Application with its Application Schema
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Rotate the client secret. The old secret stops working at once; the new one is shown once.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}/secret
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Add a Resource Type, optionally with Actions. 409 if the name exists (ignoring case).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}/resource-types
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Invoice", "actions": ["read", "approve", "export"] }

### Add an Action to a Resource Type (409 if the Resource Type is Deprecated)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}/resource-types/{{resourceTypeId}}/actions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "void" }

### Deprecate an Action. Schema entries are never removed.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}/resource-types/{{resourceTypeId}}/actions/{{actionId}}/deprecate
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Deprecate a Resource Type, and with it all its Actions
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/applications/{{applicationId}}/resource-types/{{resourceTypeId}}/deprecate
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Platform Admin actions are in the platform audit chain
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/platform/audit-events?eventType=application.registered
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
